#10700
On Bullhorn Road~
A small wooden bridge breaks up the dirt track of the Bullhorn Road, allowing
passage over a sparkling river.  On the north side of the road stands the
majestic pines that mark the edge of Spearfang Forest.  From the high point
of the bridge, you can see that the river feeds into the lake south of here.
Rocky mountains to the east can be seen through the heavy growth on either
side of the road.

